      "refersTo": "research-panel",
      "description": "Flat bordered research form surface, including the shipped field rather than invented card content.",
      "html": "<section class=\"ds-research-panel\"><label class=\"ds-field-label\" for=\"ds-panel-provider\">Which provider are you integrating?</label><div class=\"ds-research-input\"><input id=\"ds-panel-provider\" name=\"provider\" placeholder=\"A provider name or website, e.g. notion.so\" maxlength=\"160\" autocomplete=\"off\" aria-describedby=\"ds-panel-provider-help\"/></div><p class=\"ds-field-help\" id=\"ds-panel-provider-help\">Use a public provider name or URL. Never enter API keys, client secrets, or private account information.</p></section>",
      "css": ".ds-field-label{font-family:\"DM Sans Variable\",sans-serif;display:block;font-size:12px;font-weight:600;line-height:1.5;color:var(--foreground,#1c2923);margin-bottom:9px;}.ds-research-input{display:flex;align-items:center;gap:10px;border:1px solid var(--border,#e3e8e0);border-radius:7px;padding:0 13px;background:var(--canvas,#fafbf8);color:var(--muted,#627068);}.ds-research-input input{font-family:\"DM Sans Variable\",sans-serif;background:none;border:0;outline:none;color:var(--foreground,#1c2923);width:100%;min-width:0;height:44px;font-size:12px;caret-color:var(--brand,#245c45);}.ds-research-input:focus-within{outline:2px solid var(--brand,#245c45);outline-offset:2px;}.ds-field-help{font-family:\"DM Sans Variable\",sans-serif;font-size:10px;line-height:1.9;color:var(--muted,#627068);margin:10px 0 0;}.ds-research-panel{padding:28px;border:1px solid var(--border,#e3e8e0);border-radius:12px;background:var(--surface,#fff);}@media(max-width:760px){.ds-research-panel{padding:22px;}}@media(max-width:480px){.ds-research-panel{padding:18px;}}"
    }
  ],
  "narrative": {
    "northStar": "Integration field guide",
    "overview": "AuthPilot is an integration field guide inside a precise developer workspace. Forest ink, off-white paper, generous reading space, and quiet navigation give documentation a dependable place beside a code editor. The user confirmed a searchable workspace, a prominent research action, and visible evidence; premium craft and a distinct AuthPilot identity remain the direction.\n\nThe interface has two densities: an operating view for finding providers and conducting research, and a reading view for a guide. Both use the same restrained surfaces and evidence vocabulary. Confidence comes from legible requirements, attached sources, honest unknowns, and clear human handoffs.",
    "keyCharacteristics": [
      "Quiet forest and paper palette, with corresponding light and dark themes.",
      "Searchable rows for scanning; generous line height for guide claims.",
      "Evidence labels and sources next to the facts they qualify.",
      "Flat, gently rounded surfaces with visible keyboard states.",
      "Motion tied to a real interaction, loading state, or local checklist change."
    ],
    "rules": [
      {
        "name": "The Evidence Has a Name Rule.",
        "body": "Pair evidence color with its text label and icon; unknown facts retain their neutral treatment and explicit uncertainty.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Useful Accent Rule.",
        "body": "Reserve forest emphasis for actions, navigation state, evidence, links, and progress rather than decorative metrics.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Reading Measure Rule.",
        "body": "Keep guide requirement claims at 15px with 1.75 line height inside the 75ch content measure; reduce columns before shrinking reading text.",
        "section": "typography"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Flat Workspace Rule.",
        "body": "Keep resting content surfaces flat and use their border or tonal ground to separate them.",
        "section": "elevation"
      }
    ],
    "dos": [
      "**Do** preserve the forest-and-paper semantic roles in light and dark themes.",
      "**Do** attach labelled evidence, sources, and honest uncertainty to the relevant requirement.",
      "**Do** preserve the 15px/1.75 guide reading measure and collapse supporting columns on small screens.",
      "**Do** keep shared buttons and both mobile navigation controls at least 44px tall, with visible keyboard focus.",
      "**Do** show actual loading, journal events, and browser-local checklist progress, respecting reduced motion."
    ],
    "donts": [
      "**Don't** add decorative metrics, charts, heading eyebrows, or invented setup activity.",
      "**Don't** use a numeric confidence score in place of evidence labels and uncertainties.",
      "**Don't** claim provider setup, authorization, or approval was tested by this build.",
      "**Don't** apply the unused ambient shadow to resting content panels.",
      "**Don't** load provider logos from untrusted remote URLs or replace the custom mark with a text glyph."
    ]
  }
}
